  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Eight equal drops of water are falling through air with a steady speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If the drops coalesce, the new velocity is:-"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The terminal velocity can be given by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#963;</mi><mo>)</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>&#951;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Clearly,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Let the radius of the small drops be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and the radius of the big drop be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>So,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, taking the ratio<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfenced><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
